1. VISION & PURPOSE
Problem: Small businesses can't afford Starbucks-tier loyalty tech; paper cards are lost easily.

Solution: A centralized, sleek, and social loyalty app where users "collect stamps" digitally.

Scale: Expanding from Cafes to Restaurants, Fast Food, and Local Artisans.

2. USER PERSONAS
The Customer: Wants a seamless, "one-tap" experience to earn rewards. Loves gamification and "pay-it-forward" social features.

The Business Owner: Needs a simple dashboard to track loyal customers, create "Happy Hour" campaigns, and prevent fraud.

3. CORE FEATURES & LOGIC (The "Vibe" Rules)
A. The Digital Stamp (Müdavim Kart)
Logic: Every business can define its own rule (e.g., "Buy 5, Get 1 Free" or "Buy 10, Get %50 Off").

UI: Visual representation of a physical card with circles being filled.

B. The Transaction Flow (QR Logic)
User opens "My QR".

Business scans via their "Merchant Mode" (in-app).

Verification: Time-stamped, dynamic QR to prevent screenshots.

Action: Increment stamp_count in DB + Push Notification to User.

C. Social & Gamification
Pay-it-Forward: User can "Gift" a earned reward to a friend via phone number/username.

Leaderboard: "Müdavim of the Week" for each shop, rewarding the top loyalist with a badge or extra points.

D. Smart Notifications (AI/Location)
Context Aware: If user is near a registered Döner shop at 12:30 PM, send: "Lunch time! Your 5th Döner gets you a free Ayran here."

Happy Hours: Businesses can trigger "2x Stamps" during 09:00-11:00 for slow hours.

4. DESIGN VIBE (UI/UX)
Style: Modern, minimalist, "Foodie" aesthetic.

Colors: Deep Coffee Brown (for Cafes), Vibrant Orange (for Food), and Trustworthy Teal (for UI elements).

Animations: Satisfying "Stamp" sound and visual pop when a point is earned.

5. TECHNICAL CONSTRAINTS FOR AI AGENT
Architecture: Clean Architecture (MVVM).

Tech Stack Preference: Kotlin/Compose (Android) or Flutter (Cross-platform).

Auth: Google/Phone Number (Firebase).

Real-time: Use WebSockets or Firebase for instant stamp updates.